# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — MDT-Zero-Touch-Deployment
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This repository intentionally ships binaries that are required at deployment
# time: 7-Zip binaries used by the WinPE boot image, OEM app installers under
# the $OEM$ trees, LGPO.exe, MDT Templates, the AOMEI PXE Boot installer, and
# the pre-built offline media set. Those are documented as exceptions in the
# sections below.
#
# Do not weaken the ignore rules in this file to work around a specific file.
# If a file needs to be tracked, either move it into one of the intentional
# binary locations or open an issue to discuss the exception.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. MDT RUNTIME ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Created by MDT and the deployment scripts while a deployment runs on a
# target machine. They are machine-specific, can be large, and are removed
# by CleanupScripts.ps1 at the end of a successful deployment.

_SMSTaskSequence/
MININT/
LTIBootstrap.vbs
LiteTouch.lnk

# MDT-generated deployment logs — machine-specific, never committed.
BDD.log
BDD_*.log
SMSTS.log
SMSTS*.log
ZTIGather.log
ZTIDiskpart.log
ZTIApplications.log
ZTIDrivers.log
ZTIPatches.log
ZTIBackup.log
ZTIConfigure.log
ZTIDomainJoin.log
ZTIGroups.log
ZTIUserState.log
ZTIBIOSCheck.log
ZTINextPhase.log
LTIApply.log
LTISysprep.log


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. LOGS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any file ending in .log is a runtime artifact. The project does not ship
# any intentional .log files.

*.log
*.etl
*.evtx


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. CREDENTIALS AND LOCAL SECRETS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Control\Bootstrap.ini ships with generic lab defaults and is tracked by
# design. Users who edit it for a real environment must be careful not to
# commit their credentials. The rules below catch common personal overrides
# that would otherwise be silently tracked.

Control/Bootstrap.local.ini
Control/CustomSettings.local.ini
Control/Settings.local.xml
Control/Medias.local.xml
Control/*.local.ini
Control/*.local.xml

# Generic secret files that should never be tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. LARGE BINARIES — BROAD IGNORE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS images, archives, disk images, and compiled binaries are ignored
# everywhere by default. The next section explicitly re-includes the
# directories that legitimately contain binaries.

# Executables and installers
*.exe
*.com
*.scr
*.msi
*.msp
*.msu
*.cab
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.msixupload
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload

# Libraries and drivers
*.dll
*.ocx
*.cpl
*.sys
*.inf
*.cat
*.bin
*.dat
*.rom
*.efi

# Archives
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.7z.001
*.7z.002
*.7z.003
*.7z.004
*.7z.005
*.7z.006
*.7z.007
*.7z.008
*.7z.009
*.7z.010
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz

# Disk and OS images
*.iso
*.wim
*.esd
*.swm
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.avhdx
*.vmdk
*.vdi
*.ffu

# Virtual machine scratch files
*.vmsn
*.vmsd
*.vmss
*.vmx
*.vmem


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. INTENTIONAL BINARY LOCATIONS — EXPLICIT RE-INCLUDE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These directories contain binaries that MUST be tracked. They are the
# documented exceptions to the broad rules in section 4.

# WinPE boot image add-ons — 7-Zip is bundled here so the boot image can
# extract .7z archives during deployment. Required by ApplyOEMDrivers.ps1,
# ExtractOEMDrivers.ps1, and ExtractOEMApps*.ps1.
!DeploymentShare/Boot/Addon/**

# OEM content — per-architecture $OEM$ trees. Contains app installers,
# driver packages, LGPO.exe, activation scripts, and framework content.
!DeploymentShare/x64/$OEM$/**
!DeploymentShare/x86/$OEM$/**

# MDT-managed drivers — tracked only if the project ever imports a curated
# driver set. Currently empty; kept here so future imports are not blocked.
!DeploymentShare/Out-of-box Drivers/**

# Prerequisites — MDT Templates self-extractor, AOMEI PXE Boot installer,
# DHCP/WDS config templates.
!Prerequisites/**

# Offline media — the pre-built MDT media set with SWM-split OS images.
!MDT/**/**


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files Windows creates automatically when browsing a folder. Never commit.

Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.url
*.stackdump
[Dd]esktop.ini


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. macOS AND LINUX JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contributors using non-Windows editors or running the repo through a
# cross-platform toolchain.

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
*.swp
*.swo
*~


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. TEMPORARY AND BACKUP FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.crdownload
*.partial
*.part
~$*
*.dmp


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. EDITOR AND IDE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings and workspace files from common editors. Users keep their own
# local settings; they are not part of the project.

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json.example
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json.example

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

*.code-workspace


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. POWERSHELL AND SCRIPT ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.ps1xml
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1.local
TestResults.xml
CodeCoverage.xml
*.Tests.ps1.bak


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11. PERSONAL AND SCRATCH FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything a user creates locally that is not part of the project.

notes/
scratch/
sandbox/
*.personal.*
*.private.*
*.draft.*


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 12. GIT INTERNAL BACKUPS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.gitattributes.bak
.gitmodules.bak
*.orig.git
*.orig.gitignore


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13. FINAL OVERRIDES — FILES THAT MUST ALWAYS BE TRACKED
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Re-include files that would otherwise be caught by the broad rules above.

# Keep .gitkeep placeholders so empty directory structures are tracked.
!.gitkeep
!**/.gitkeep

# Documentation assets — screenshots, diagrams, sample output.
!docs/images/**
!docs/examples/**

# Configuration and metadata files that must be tracked in the deployment
# share and offline media set.
!DeploymentShare/Control/**
!DeploymentShare/Scripts/**
!DeploymentShare/Operating Systems/*.xml
!DeploymentShare/Task Sequences/**
!MDT/Content/Deploy/**


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END OF .gitignore
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If you need to force-add a file that this file ignores, use:
#
#     git add -f <file>
#
# and explain WHY in your commit message and pull request description.
# The reviewer will decide whether the file belongs in section 5 or should
# be relocated to one of the intentional binary locations.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
